pass unchanged. Post-merge: recheck posted on change 1309 to clear the red-main Verified-1.","timestamp":1785790524863508001}],"created_at":1785788799629249001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"48025204-6593-41c4-aa99-699b966576a3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"},{"link_uuid":"6107e77e-392b-4ea4-a422-6a446383214c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6e9d-b7d5-4921-4225"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nCommit 1d75850974 (ticket f124, 'close the ambient-default provider leak') landed ~10 minutes after the comment-hygiene gate itself (f2b2d0b410, ticket b047) via concurrent Gerrit review — its comments cite a bare GitHub Actions run id three times, which the new whole-tree gate rejects. Every change pushed after 1d75850974 now fails CI's lint job (observed: change 1309 ps4, change 1311 ps3), i.e. main is red for everyone.\n\n## Approach\nReplace the three bare run-id citations with durable prose citing ticket f124 (the incident's ticket, per the gate's own teaching message. Sites: tests/external/test_provider_matrix_live.py:56, tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:22, tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:157.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py exits 0 on the tree\n- [x] the three comments still convey the same incident evidence (provider leak shipped while class-only assertion passed), now citing f124","detected_by":"agent","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6e9d-b7d5-4921-4225"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6d1ff93c-1c22-4346-a3bd-6df375238e31","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5f60-22fd-48af-4704","ticket_type":"bug","title":"comment-hygiene gate red on main: f124 run-